But PM's export spec bases use Chinese with spaces e.g. `PERMANOVA 结果`? Let me check the export bases for all three to keep the "格式" decision coherent. The user asked "这三个模板名称统一一下文件名格式" — only the *template* download names need unifying. But if I change only templates while exports remain 空格/下划线混用, that's half-done. Let me look at the export bases quickly and decide: unify template names to the underscore style, and report the export-name inconsistency (maybe unify too if cheap — the med harness asserts exact export prefixes 'PERMANOVA-med 结果|分组置换检验|...' so changing them breaks tests + user expectations. Since the user only asked about 模板, I'll unify 模板 (all three) and leave 结果/输入 names, but note that `下载输入` names differ in separator style; actually those ARE worth unifying too... careful: test assertions pin med's export prefixes; med's 输入 name `PERMANOVA-med 输入_` isn't asserted? In test_med_view the 5 prefixes include 'PERMANOVA-med 输入'. So changing it requires updating the test. Hmm.

Decision (ask-free, minimal surprise): unify the three **模板** filenames to `<slug> 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx` (space between slug and 用途, underscore before stamp) — this keeps Med/PM's existing style (space + Chinese 用途), only changing NR's `Non-random-PERMANOVA_数据模板.xlsx` → `Non-random-PERMANOVA 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx`. Wait, that changes 2 of 3 files' names for the user. Alternative: keep NR's style and change PM/Med to `PERMANOVA 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx` & `PERMANOVA-med 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx` and NR → `Non-random-PERMANOVA 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx`: i.e. **统一为 `<slug> 数据模板_<stamp>.xlsx`**，slug 各自保持现状（`PERMANOVA` / `PERMANOVA-med` / `Non-random-PERMANOVA`）。That's a clean rule: 用途词一律「数据模板」，一律带时间戳，分隔符一律「空格 + 下划线」。I'll do that and also make it a spec-level constant so the three views can't drift again: put `templateFileName(slug, stamp)`... Simplest: each view builds `${slug} 数据模板_${this.stamp()}.xlsx`; to prevent drift, define the pattern once in sheetIo.js: `export function templateFilename(slug, stamp) { return `${slug} 数据模板_${stamp}.xlsx`; }` and have all three call it, plus a harness asserting all three specs/views produce names matching one regex. Good — that's "L1 认识形状不认识业务" compatible (it's a naming primitive).

Then the tests: assert each view's downloadTemplate filename via the pattern (unit: check the view source binds it? Better: call `templateFilename` with the three slugs and assert the regex; and in each view harness assert that `downloadTemplate` uses `templateFilename(` + the right slug — static but cheap. Even better: make the views expose the filename via a computed/method `templateFileName()` so tests can call it and assert the exact string. That's cleaner design too (no string built inline in an IO call).

I'll implement: `templateFilename(slug, stamp)` in sheetIo.js; each view gets `templateFileName()` method returning `templateFilename('PERMANOVA', this.stamp())` etc.; downloadTemplate uses it; harnesses assert the exact names + shared pattern across the three modules (a cross-module test in test_sheet_io or a new small one in test_home_status? better in test_sheet_io as "命名原语" + per-view assertions in each view harness).

